  "class_note": "The confusion classes are built from Azure's IPA phoneme symbols. The en-US pass returned them; the en-GB pass, which replaced it on 2026-09-14, returns them EMPTY — 550 empty symbols across every rescored record against 0 in the two that still hold two-pass data. So i/ii, schwa, s/z, cat/cut and j/y currently have no source and only the spelling-derived classes (th, b/v, -ed, s-cluster, h) survive. `phonemes_before_2026_09_16` keeps the old tallies, but they were counted against a reference that was a fraction of what he read, so they are not a correct baseline either — they are kept so nothing is destroyed, not because they are right. plan-from-ledger.py reads these classes: the Minimal Pairs weights are downstream of this.",
  "locale_note": "SCORING LOCALE CHANGED TO en-US ON 2026-09-16, at the user's decision. Microsoft's docs make en-US the only locale that returns prosody AND named IPA phonemes; the en-GB single pass run from 09-14 to 09-16 returned 550 empty phoneme names and an undocumented prosody number. The six reads of 09-10 to 09-16 are en-GB and are a CLOSED series: nothing after this date joins them. They were not rescored again in en-US — that would be a third pass over the same 197 minutes of audio against a free tier already spent, to give six points a new baseline that tomorrow's reads will build on anyway."
